From d7d70b2630df44f289f92d5bc340f3a79e563420 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:49:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Check this setup: the card "3D: frame packing" asks the
 driver first

Before its 3D clip, the card asks the driver, through Kodi's builtin
HadesFramePackingCheck, whether it takes the HDMI 3D frame-packed mode
that the display declares, with the buffers that a 3D video would go
out in, in test commits only: nothing changes on the screen. What it
answered is said after what became of the clip: taken (and how the
picture gets into the buffers: drawn by the graphics card, or copied
by the processor where it cannot draw into them), refused (and why,
from the driver's own kernel lines, or what the test commit answered),
no frame-packed mode for a display that declares 3D, not asked while
a video plays, or no answer from Kodi. The summary line of a
diagnostic report has the whole answer. A reason of the driver that
its refusal without a picture said already is not said again for the
clip. English, and Spanish of Spain, Argentina and Mexico.
---
